IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg5-s221-s224-bonds-and-records`
IMPORT `dg5-s222-s229-s230-notice-of-meetings`
IMPORT `dg5-s223-s225-s227-directors-and-courts`
IMPORT `dg5-s228-consent-in-lieu-of-meeting`
IMPORT `dg5-s231-inspectors`
IMPORT `dg5-s232-s233-delivery-of-notice`
IMPORT `dg5-s241-s242-amendment`
IMPORT `dg5-s243-s245-capital-and-restatement`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, sections 221 to 233 and 241 to 246 -- THE SEAT LAYER (piece dg5).
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation under the General Corporation Law:
-- an incorporator, a director or officer, a stockholder (including a minority stockholder). The person asks what the Law lets them do, what it requires of them,
-- what they may require of the corporation, and what can be done to them. The Secretary of State, the Court of Chancery and the Attorney General get no seat:
-- their acts appear here only as what they mean for the person (for example "may the Court order an election if I ask?").
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date or a choice the layer-1 modules already define -- one for each fact the person can state,
-- each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked. The records the layer-1 modules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers,
-- and the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is restated here. A record field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying so.
-- Nothing here is new law.
--
-- WHERE THE LAW LEAVES IT TO THE CERTIFICATE OF INCORPORATION OR THE BYLAWS. The Law often says "unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws".
-- The person is asked "does the certificate or the bylaws say otherwise?"; the layer-1 rule takes the core's `Where a provision is made` and the seat gives it
-- `in the certificate of incorporation` for yes and `in none of these` for no (the two places the Law names in the sections of this piece).
--
-- WHAT THE PERSON CANNOT STATE. Judgments the Law hands to the Court of Chancery ("if the Court determines", "may order") are asked as conditional facts
-- ("has the Court determined that ...?"). The kinds of corporation are asked as "is it a stock corporation?" and "is it a charitable nonstock corporation?":
-- the two nonstock kinds that are not charitable are not told apart by any rule of this piece.
--
-- Questions are grouped under the section of the Law that answers them, in the text's order. Where a group arises only in a situation the person may not be in,
-- the heading says so, so that the form can ask "Has this happened to you?" first.

§ `Section 221 -- the rights of holders of bonds, debentures and other obligations`

-- Helpers: not questions. They only build the kind of corporation and the place a provision is made from yes/no answers.
GIVEN stock IS A BOOLEAN
      charitable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Kind of corporation`
`dg5 seat the kind of corporation` stock charitable MEANS
    IF stock
    THEN `a stock corporation`
    ELSE IF charitable
         THEN `a charitable nonstock corporation`
         ELSE `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`

GIVEN otherwise IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Where a provision is made`
`dg5 seat where the provision is made` otherwise MEANS
    IF otherwise THEN `in the certificate of incorporation` ELSE `in none of these`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `dg5 s 221 Holder of obligations of the corporation`
`dg5 seat holder of obligations` a b c d e MEANS
    `dg5 s 221 Holder of obligations of the corporation` WITH
          `the person holds bonds, debentures or other obligations issued or to be issued by the corporation` IS a
        , `the certificate of incorporation confers the power to vote in respect to the corporate affairs and management` IS b
        , `the certificate of incorporation confers the same right of inspection of the books, accounts and other records that the stockholders have` IS c
        , `the certificate of incorporation confers another right that the stockholders have` IS d
        , `the certificate of incorporation provides that the holders of obligations are deemed to be stockholders` IS e

-- s 221. A corporation may give the holders of its bonds, debentures or other obligations a vote on its affairs, the stockholders' right of inspection, other stockholders' rights,
-- and may deem them stockholders for the stockholder votes the Law requires -- but only if its certificate of incorporation says so.
@export Can I vote on the corporation's affairs as a holder of its bonds, debentures or other obligations (s 221)?
GIVEN `I hold bonds, debentures or other obligations of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold bonds, debentures or other obligations that the corporation has issued or is to issue?
      `the certificate gives holders of obligations the power to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation's certificate of incorporation give the holders of its obligations the power to vote on its affairs and management?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I vote on the corporation's affairs as a holder of its obligations (s 221)` IF
    `s 221 the holder of obligations may vote on the corporate affairs and management`
        (`dg5 seat holder of obligations` `I hold bonds, debentures or other obligations of the corporation` `the certificate gives holders of obligations the power to vote`
            -- Placeholders: the voting rule does not read the other three fields.
            FALSE FALSE FALSE)

@export Do I have a stockholder's right of inspection as a holder of the corporation's obligations (s 221)?
GIVEN `I hold bonds, debentures or other obligations of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold bonds, debentures or other obligations that the corporation has issued or is to issue?
      `the certificate gives holders of obligations the stockholders' right of inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation give the holders of obligations the same right to inspect the books, accounts and other records that stockholders have?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a stockholder's right of inspection as a holder of the corporation's obligations (s 221)` IF
    `s 221 the holder of obligations has the stockholders' right of inspection`
        (`dg5 seat holder of obligations` `I hold bonds, debentures or other obligations of the corporation`
            -- Placeholder: the inspection rule does not read the voting field.
            FALSE
            `the certificate gives holders of obligations the stockholders' right of inspection`
            -- Placeholders: nor the other two.
            FALSE FALSE)

@export Am I treated as a stockholder for a stockholder vote as a holder of the corporation's obligations (s 221)?
GIVEN `I hold bonds, debentures or other obligations of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold bonds, debentures or other obligations that the corporation has issued or is to issue?
      `the certificate says holders of obligations are deemed stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation say that the holders of the corporation's obligations are deemed to be stockholders (and their obligations shares of stock) for votes of stockholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as a stockholder for a stockholder vote as a holder of the corporation's obligations (s 221)` IF
    `s 221 the holder of obligations is deemed a stockholder, and the obligation a share of stock, for a vote of stockholders required by the chapter`
        (`dg5 seat holder of obligations` `I hold bonds, debentures or other obligations of the corporation`
            -- Placeholders: the deeming rule reads only the first and the last field.
            FALSE FALSE FALSE
            `the certificate says holders of obligations are deemed stockholders`)

@export Can the certificate take away my right as a stockholder to vote on this matter (s 221)?
GIVEN `the certificate takes away the right of holders of capital stock to vote on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation take away, in whole or in part, the holders of capital stock's right to vote on this matter?
      `my class votes as a class on this matter under s 242(b)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter an amendment of the certificate that would increase or decrease the number of authorized shares of your class or its par value, or adversely change the powers, preferences or special rights of your class or series (so that your class or series votes as a class)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the certificate take away my right as a stockholder to vote on this matter (s 221)` IF
    `s 221 the holder of capital stock has been divested of the right to vote on the matter` `the certificate takes away the right of holders of capital stock to vote on the matter` `my class votes as a class on this matter under s 242(b)(2)`

§ `Section 222 -- notice of stockholders' meetings`

-- s 222(a), (b). The stockholder's side: notice is owed to each stockholder entitled to vote as of the record date for notice, whenever stockholders may act at a meeting.
@export Must the corporation give me notice of the stockholders' meeting (s 222)?
GIVEN `stockholders are required or permitted to act at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are stockholders required or permitted to take any action at the meeting?
      `I was a stockholder on the record date for notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a stockholder on the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting?
      `I am entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to vote at the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation give me notice of the stockholders' meeting (s 222)` IF
        `s 222(a) a notice of the meeting must be given` `stockholders are required or permitted to act at the meeting`
    AND `s 222(b) the stockholder must be given the notice of the meeting` `I was a stockholder on the record date for notice` `I am entitled to vote at the meeting`

-- s 222(b), the other side of the same relation: the officer or director who has to give the notice.
@export Must we give this stockholder notice of the stockholders' meeting (s 222)?
GIVEN `stockholders are required or permitted to act at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are stockholders required or permitted to take any action at the meeting?
      `the person was a stockholder on the record date for notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person a stockholder on the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting?
      `the person is entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person entitled to vote at the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we give this stockholder notice of the stockholders' meeting (s 222)` IF
        `s 222(a) a notice of the meeting must be given` `stockholders are required or permitted to act at the meeting`
    AND `s 222(b) the stockholder must be given the notice of the meeting` `the person was a stockholder on the record date for notice` `the person is entitled to vote at the meeting`

@export Was the notice of the meeting given early enough, and not too early (s 222)?
GIVEN `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of the meeting given (under section 232)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-15)
      `another section sets a different time for this notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another section of the Law (for example the merger sections) set a different time for notice of this meeting?
      `the shortest number of days before the meeting that section allows` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what is the fewest days before the meeting that section allows the notice to be given? (0 if there is no such section)
      `the longest number of days before the meeting that section allows` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what is the greatest number of days before the meeting that section allows the notice to be given? (0 if there is no such section)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the notice of the meeting given early enough, and not too early (s 222)` IS
    `s 222(b) the notice was given within the time allowed` (JUST `the date the notice was given`) `the date of the meeting` `the time another section allows`
    WHERE
        `the time another section allows` MEANS
            IF `another section sets a different time for this notice`
            THEN JUST (`dg5 s 222(b) Time allowed for a notice` WITH
                           `the shortest time before the meeting that the notice may be given` IS `period in days` `the shortest number of days before the meeting that section allows`
                         , `the longest time before the meeting that the notice may be given`  IS `period in days` `the longest number of days before the meeting that section allows`)
            ELSE NOTHING

-- s 222(a). What the notice has to say.
@export Does the notice of the meeting say everything it must (s 222)?
GIVEN `the meeting is a special meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting a special meeting?
      `the meeting has a place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the meeting be held at a place?
      `stockholders and proxy holders may be deemed present and vote by remote communications` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can stockholders and proxy holders be deemed present in person and vote by remote communications?
      `the voting record date differs from the notice record date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the record date for determining who may vote different from the record date for determining who is entitled to notice?
      `the notice states the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the place of the meeting?
      `the notice states the date and hour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the date and hour of the meeting?
      `the notice states the means of remote communications` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the means of remote communications?
      `the notice states the voting record date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote?
      `the notice states the purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the purpose or purposes for which the meeting is called?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the notice of the meeting say everything it must (s 222)` IF
    `s 222(a) the notice of the meeting states what it must` `the notice`
    WHERE
        `the notice` MEANS `dg5 s 222(a) Notice of a meeting of stockholders` WITH
              `the meeting is a special meeting` IS `the meeting is a special meeting`
            , `the meeting has a place` IS `the meeting has a place`
            , `stockholders and proxy holders may be deemed present in person and vote by remote communications` IS `stockholders and proxy holders may be deemed present and vote by remote communications`
            , `the record date for voting differs from the record date for notice` IS `the voting record date differs from the notice record date`
            , `the notice states the place of the meeting` IS `the notice states the place`
            , `the notice states the date and hour of the meeting` IS `the notice states the date and hour`
            , `the notice states the means of remote communications` IS `the notice states the means of remote communications`
            , `the notice states the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote` IS `the notice states the voting record date`
            , `the notice states the purpose or purposes for which the meeting is called` IS `the notice states the purposes`

-- s 222(c). The adjourned meeting.
§§ `If a meeting has been adjourned (section 222(c))`

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
      an IS A BOOLEAN
      di IS A BOOLEAN
      sf IS A BOOLEAN
      d1 IS A DATE
      d2 IS A DATE
      nr IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `dg5 s 222(c) Adjournment of a meeting`
`dg5 seat adjournment` b an di sf d1 d2 nr MEANS
    `dg5 s 222(c) Adjournment of a meeting` WITH
          `the bylaws require notice of the adjourned meeting` IS b
        , `the time, place and means of remote communications of the adjourned meeting were announced at the meeting at which the adjournment was taken` IS an
        , `the time, place and means of remote communications of the adjourned meeting were displayed during the time scheduled for the meeting on the electronic network used for remote participation` IS di
        , `the time, place and means of remote communications of the adjourned meeting were set forth in the notice of the meeting given under s 222(a)` IS sf
        , `the date of the meeting that was adjourned` IS d1
        , `the date of the adjourned meeting` IS d2
        , `a new record date for stockholders entitled to vote was fixed for the adjourned meeting` IS nr

@export Must I be given notice of the adjourned meeting (s 222(c))?
GIVEN `the bylaws require notice of an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the bylaws require notice of an adjourned meeting?
      `the adjourned meeting was announced at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the time, place and means of remote communications of the adjourned meeting announced at the meeting at which the adjournment was taken?
      `the adjourned meeting was displayed on the electronic network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they displayed, during the time scheduled for the meeting, on the same electronic network used for remote participation?
      `the adjourned meeting was set forth in the notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they set forth in the notice of the original meeting?
      `the date of the meeting that was adjourned` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the meeting that was adjourned? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
      `the date of the adjourned meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the adjourned meeting to be held? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-15)
      `a new voting record date was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a new record date for stockholders entitled to vote fixed for the adjourned meeting?
      `I was a stockholder of record entitled to vote at the adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a stockholder of record entitled to vote at the adjourned meeting as of the record date that applies (the record date for notice of the adjourned meeting, if a new one was fixed)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be given notice of the adjourned meeting (s 222(c))` IF
    `s 222(c) the stockholder must be given notice of the adjourned meeting`
        (`dg5 seat adjournment` `the bylaws require notice of an adjourned meeting` `the adjourned meeting was announced at the meeting` `the adjourned meeting was displayed on the electronic network` `the adjourned meeting was set forth in the notice of the meeting` `the date of the meeting that was adjourned` `the date of the adjourned meeting` `a new voting record date was fixed`)
        `I was a stockholder of record entitled to vote at the adjourned meeting`

@export Must we give notice of the adjourned meeting (s 222(c))?
GIVEN `the bylaws require notice of an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the bylaws require notice of an adjourned meeting?
      `the adjourned meeting was announced at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the time, place and means of remote communications of the adjourned meeting announced at the meeting at which the adjournment was taken?
      `the adjourned meeting was displayed on the electronic network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they displayed, during the time scheduled for the meeting, on the same electronic network used for remote participation?
      `the adjourned meeting was set forth in the notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they set forth in the notice of the original meeting?
      `the date of the meeting that was adjourned` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the meeting that was adjourned? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
      `the date of the adjourned meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the adjourned meeting to be held? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-15)
      `a new voting record date was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a new record date for stockholders entitled to vote fixed for the adjourned meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we give notice of the adjourned meeting (s 222(c))` IF
    `s 222(c) notice of the adjourned meeting must be given`
        (`dg5 seat adjournment` `the bylaws require notice of an adjourned meeting` `the adjourned meeting was announced at the meeting` `the adjourned meeting was displayed on the electronic network` `the adjourned meeting was set forth in the notice of the meeting` `the date of the meeting that was adjourned` `the date of the adjourned meeting` `a new voting record date was fixed`)

@export As a director, must the board fix a new record date for notice of the adjourned meeting (s 222(c))?
GIVEN `a new voting record date was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a new record date for stockholders entitled to vote fixed for the adjourned meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a director, must the board fix a new record date for notice of the adjourned meeting (s 222(c))` IF
    `s 222(c) the board of directors must fix a new record date for notice of the adjourned meeting`
        (`dg5 seat adjournment`
            -- Placeholders: the rule reads only whether a new voting record date was fixed.
            FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) `a new voting record date was fixed`)

@export May the corporation transact at the adjourned meeting the business that could have been transacted at the original meeting (s 222(c))?
GIVEN `the business could have been transacted at the original meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it business that might have been transacted at the original meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation transact at the adjourned meeting the business that could have been transacted at the original meeting (s 222(c))` IF
    `s 222(c) the corporation may transact the business at the adjourned meeting` `the business could have been transacted at the original meeting`

§ `Section 223 -- vacancies and newly created directorships`

-- s 223(a). Vacancies are filled by the directors in office unless the certificate or bylaws provide otherwise.
@export Have the directors validly filled the vacancy or newly created directorship (s 223(a))?
GIVEN `the seat is one elected by all the stockholders voting as a single class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the vacant or new seat one for a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote, as a single class?
      `the seat is one elected by a class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it instead a seat for a director elected by a class or series of stock that the certificate entitles to elect one or more directors?
      `the certificate or the bylaws provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide a different way of filling it?
      `the filling complies with that provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, was the vacancy filled as that provision requires?
      `the number of directors in office who may fill the seat` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors are in office who may fill it (all directors in office for a single-class seat; the directors elected by the class or series for a class seat)?
      `the number of those directors who vote to fill it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them vote to fill it (a sole remaining director counts as 1 of 1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the directors validly filled the vacancy or newly created directorship (s 223(a))` IS
    `s 223(a) the directors have filled the vacancy in the manner the section provides` `the filling`
    WHERE
        `the filling` MEANS `dg5 s 223(a) Filling of a vacancy by the directors` WITH
              `the directorship being filled under section 223(a)` IS
                  IF `the seat is one elected by all the stockholders voting as a single class`
                  THEN `a directorship of a director elected by all the stockholders having the right to vote as a single class`
                  ELSE IF `the seat is one elected by a class or series`
                       THEN `a directorship of a director elected by the holders of a class or series who are entitled to elect 1 or more directors by the certificate of incorporation`
                       ELSE `a directorship of some other kind that section 223(a) does not describe`
            , `where a provision otherwise providing is made` IS `dg5 seat where the provision is made` `the certificate or the bylaws provide otherwise`
            , `the filling complies with the provision otherwise providing` IS `the filling complies with that provision`
            , `the number of directors in office who may fill the directorship` IS `the number of directors in office who may fill the seat`
            , `the number of those directors who vote to fill it, or act as the sole remaining director` IS `the number of those directors who vote to fill it`

§§ `If the corporation has no directors in office (section 223(a))`

GIVEN officer IS A BOOLEAN
      stockholder IS A BOOLEAN
      fiduciary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `dg5 s 223(a) Person who may act when there are no directors`
`dg5 seat person who may act when there are no directors` officer stockholder fiduciary MEANS
    IF officer
    THEN `an officer of the corporation, acting where there are no directors`
    ELSE IF stockholder
         THEN `a stockholder, acting where there are no directors`
         ELSE IF fiduciary
              THEN `an executor, administrator, trustee or guardian of a stockholder, or other fiduciary entrusted with like responsibility for the person or estate of a stockholder`
              ELSE `someone else, who may not act where there are no directors`

@export May I call a special meeting of stockholders to elect directors when the corporation has none (s 223(a))?
GIVEN `I am an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the corporation?
      `I am a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder of the corporation?
      `I am an executor, administrator, trustee, guardian or other fiduciary of a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an executor, administrator, trustee or guardian of a stockholder, or another fiduciary entrusted with like responsibility for the person or estate of a stockholder?
      `the corporation has no directors in office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have no directors in office (by reason of death, resignation or other cause)?
      `the call is in accordance with the certificate or the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the call be made in accordance with the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I call a special meeting of stockholders to elect directors when the corporation has none (s 223(a))` IF
    `s 223(a) the person may call a special meeting of stockholders`
        (`dg5 seat person who may act when there are no directors` `I am an officer of the corporation` `I am a stockholder` `I am an executor, administrator, trustee, guardian or other fiduciary of a stockholder`)
        `the corporation has no directors in office` `the call is in accordance with the certificate or the bylaws`

@export May I ask the Court of Chancery to order an election when the corporation has no directors (s 223(a))?
GIVEN `I am an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the corporation?
      `I am a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder of the corporation?
      `I am an executor, administrator, trustee, guardian or other fiduciary of a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an executor, administrator, trustee or guardian of a stockholder, or another fiduciary entrusted with like responsibility for the person or estate of a stockholder?
      `the corporation has no directors in office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have no directors in office (by reason of death, resignation or other cause)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Court of Chancery to order an election when the corporation has no directors (s 223(a))` IF
    `s 223(a) the person may apply to the Court of Chancery for a decree summarily ordering an election`
        (`dg5 seat person who may act when there are no directors` `I am an officer of the corporation` `I am a stockholder` `I am an executor, administrator, trustee, guardian or other fiduciary of a stockholder`)
        `the corporation has no directors in office`

§§ `If a director has been chosen to fill a vacancy, or the board is short of directors (section 223(b) to (d))`

@export Until when does a director chosen to fill a vacancy hold office (s 223(b))?
GIVEN `the directors are divided into classes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the corporation's directors divided into classes?
      `the date of the next election of the class` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the next election of the class for which the director was chosen? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-05-20)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Until when does a director chosen to fill a vacancy hold office (s 223(b))` IS
    `s 223(b) the date until which the director chosen holds office, and until a successor is elected and qualified` `the directors are divided into classes` `the date of the next election of the class`

@export May I, as a stockholder with enough stock, ask the Court of Chancery to order an election to fill vacancies (s 223(c))?
GIVEN `the number of directors in office when the vacancy was filled` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors were in office when the vacancy or newly created directorship was filled?
      `the number of directors of the whole board before any increase` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors did the whole board have, as constituted immediately before any increase?
      `the votes I and the other applicants hold` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes of voting stock do you and the other applicants hold together?
      `the votes outstanding that may vote for such directors` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes of voting stock are outstanding and have the right to vote for such directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as a stockholder with enough stock, ask the Court of Chancery to order an election to fill vacancies (s 223(c))` IS
    `s 223(c) the stockholders may apply to the Court of Chancery to order an election` `the number of directors in office when the vacancy was filled` `the number of directors of the whole board before any increase` `the votes I and the other applicants hold` `the votes outstanding that may vote for such directors`

@export Can the directors fill a vacancy before a resigning director's resignation takes effect (s 223(d))?
GIVEN `the certificate or the bylaws provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide a different way of filling it?
      `the filling complies with that provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, was the vacancy filled as that provision requires?
      `the number of directors in office including those who have resigned` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors are in office, counting those who have resigned effective at a future date?
      `the number of those directors who vote to fill it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them vote to fill the vacancy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the directors fill a vacancy before a resigning director's resignation takes effect (s 223(d))` IS
    `s 223(d) the directors may fill the vacancy before the resignation takes effect` (`dg5 seat where the provision is made` `the certificate or the bylaws provide otherwise`) `the filling complies with that provision` `the number of directors in office including those who have resigned` `the number of those directors who vote to fill it`

§ `Section 224 -- keeping the corporation's records`

-- s 224. The corporation may keep its records on any information storage device or electronic network, if they can be turned into clear paper within a reasonable time
-- and, for the stock ledger, can serve the stockholder list, record what the Law requires and record transfers.
@export May the corporation keep its records in electronic form (s 224)?
GIVEN `the records are kept in an information storage device, method or electronic network or database` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the records kept on, or by means of, an information storage device, method, or one or more electronic networks or databases?
      `the records can be converted into clearly legible paper form within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the records be converted into clearly legible paper form within a reasonable time?
      `the records are the stock ledger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are these the records of the stock ledger?
      `the stock ledger can be used to prepare the list of stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the stock ledger be used to prepare the list of stockholders required by sections 219 and 220?
      `the stock ledger records the information the Law specifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the stock ledger record the information specified in sections 156, 159, 217(a) and 218?
      `the stock ledger records transfers of stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the stock ledger record transfers of stock as governed by Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation keep its records in electronic form (s 224)` IF
    `s 224 the records may be kept in that form` `the records`
    WHERE
        `the records` MEANS `dg5 s 224 Records kept by the corporation` WITH
              `the records are kept on, or by means of, or in the form of, an information storage device, method, or 1 or more electronic networks or databases` IS `the records are kept in an information storage device, method or electronic network or database`
            , `the records can be converted into clearly legible paper form within a reasonable time` IS `the records can be converted into clearly legible paper form within a reasonable time`
            , `the records are the stock ledger` IS `the records are the stock ledger`
            , `the stock ledger can be used to prepare the list of stockholders specified in ss 219 and 220` IS `the stock ledger can be used to prepare the list of stockholders`
            , `the stock ledger records the information specified in ss 156, 159, 217(a) and 218` IS `the stock ledger records the information the Law specifies`
            , `the stock ledger records transfers of stock as governed by Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6` IS `the stock ledger records transfers of stock`

@export Must the corporation give me its records on paper if I ask (s 224)?
GIVEN `the records are kept in a form that section 224 allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the records kept in electronic or other storage form that section 224 allows (they can be converted into clearly legible paper within a reasonable time)?
      `I am entitled to inspect the records under a provision of the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to inspect these records under a provision of the General Corporation Law (for example as a stockholder under section 220)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation give me its records on paper if I ask (s 224)` IF
    `s 224 the corporation must convert the records into clearly legible paper form on the person's request` `the records are kept in a form that section 224 allows` `I am entitled to inspect the records under a provision of the Law`

@export Is the paper copy of the corporation's records as good as the original in evidence (s 224)?
GIVEN `the records are kept in a form that section 224 allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the records kept in a form that section 224 allows?
      `the paper copy accurately portrays the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the paper copy accurately portray the record?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the paper copy of the corporation's records as good as the original in evidence (s 224)` IF
    `s 224 the paper form is valid and admissible in evidence and accepted for all other purposes to the same extent as an original paper record` `the records are kept in a form that section 224 allows` `the paper copy accurately portrays the record`

§ `Section 225 -- contested elections, and proceedings in the Court of Chancery`

GIVEN stockholder IS A BOOLEAN
      director IS A BOOLEAN
      officer IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `dg5 s 225 Applicant to the Court of Chancery`
`dg5 seat applicant` stockholder director officer MEANS
    IF stockholder
    THEN `a stockholder, applying under section 225`
    ELSE IF director
         THEN `a director, applying under section 225`
         ELSE IF officer
              THEN `an officer of the corporation whose title to office is contested`
              ELSE `someone else, who may not apply under section 225`

@export May I ask the Court of Chancery to decide who is validly a director or officer (s 225(a))?
GIVEN `I am a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder of the corporation?
      `I am a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the corporation?
      `I am an officer whose title to office is contested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer whose title to office is contested?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Court of Chancery to decide who is validly a director or officer (s 225(a))` IF
    `s 225(a) the applicant may apply to the Court of Chancery to determine the validity of an election, appointment, removal or resignation`
        (`dg5 seat applicant` `I am a stockholder` `I am a director` `I am an officer whose title to office is contested`)

@export May I ask the Court of Chancery to decide the result of a stockholder vote (s 225(b))?
GIVEN `I am a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder of the corporation?
      `the application is made by the corporation itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made by the corporation itself?
      `the vote was on a matter other than the election of directors or officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vote of stockholders on a matter other than the election of directors or officers?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Court of Chancery to decide the result of a stockholder vote (s 225(b))` IF
    `s 225(b) the applicant may apply to the Court of Chancery to determine the result of the vote of stockholders`
        (IF `the application is made by the corporation itself`
         THEN `the corporation itself, applying under section 225`
         ELSE IF `I am a stockholder` THEN `a stockholder, applying under section 225` ELSE `someone else, who may not apply under section 225`)
        `the vote was on a matter other than the election of directors or officers`

@export Must another party be joined for the Court to decide the result of the vote (s 225(b))?
GIVEN `the application is under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one under section 225(b), about the result of a stockholder vote?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must another party be joined for the Court to decide the result of the vote (s 225(b))` IS
    IF `the application is under subsection (b)`
    THEN JUST `s 225(b) another party must be joined for the Court to adjudicate the result of the vote`
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN c IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `dg5 s 225 Kind of application`
`dg5 seat kind of application` c b MEANS
    IF c
    THEN `an application under subsection (c) of section 225 to remove a director`
    ELSE IF b
         THEN `an application under subsection (b) of section 225 about the result of a vote of stockholders`
         ELSE `an application under subsection (a) of section 225 about an election, appointment, removal or resignation`

@export Is service on the registered agent treated as service on me (s 225)?
GIVEN `the application is to remove a director under subsection (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one to remove a director under section 225(c)?
      `the application is about the result of a vote under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one about the result of a stockholder vote under section 225(b)?
      `I am the person whose title to office is contested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person whose title to office is contested?
      `I am the person claiming the office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person (if any) claiming the contested office?
      `I am a director whose removal is sought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director whose removal is sought?
      `the application was served upon the registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the application served upon the corporation's registered agent?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is service on the registered agent treated as service on me (s 225)` IF
    `s 225 service upon the registered agent is deemed service upon the party` (`dg5 seat kind of application` `the application is to remove a director under subsection (c)` `the application is about the result of a vote under subsection (b)`) `me` `the application was served upon the registered agent`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS
            IF `I am the person whose title to office is contested`
            THEN `the person whose title to office is contested`
            ELSE IF `I am the person claiming the office`
                 THEN `the person, if any, claiming the office`
                 ELSE IF `I am a director whose removal is sought`
                      THEN `the director or directors whose removal is sought`
                      ELSE `another person, who is not a party named in section 225`

@export As the registered agent, must I forward a copy of the application immediately (s 225)?
GIVEN `the application is to remove a director under subsection (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one to remove a director under section 225(c)?
      `the application is about the result of a vote under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one about the result of a stockholder vote under section 225(b)?
      `the application was served upon me as the registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the application served upon you as the corporation's registered agent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the registered agent, must I forward a copy of the application immediately (s 225)` IS
    `s 225 the registered agent must forward a copy of the application immediately` (`dg5 seat kind of application` `the application is to remove a director under subsection (c)` `the application is about the result of a vote under subsection (b)`) `the application was served upon me as the registered agent`

@export Was the copy forwarded to me in the way the Law requires (s 225)?
GIVEN `the copy was sent in a postpaid, sealed, registered letter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the copy sent in a postpaid, sealed, registered letter?
      `the letter was addressed to my last known address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter addressed to the post-office address last known to the registered agent, or furnished to the agent by the applicant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the copy forwarded to me in the way the Law requires (s 225)` IF
    `s 225 the registered agent has forwarded the copy in the manner the section requires` `the copy was sent in a postpaid, sealed, registered letter` `the letter was addressed to my last known address`

@export What can the Court of Chancery do on an application about an election (s 225(a))?
GIVEN `the power` IS A `dg5 s 225(a) Power of the Court of Chancery on an application` @desc Which power? One of: to hear and determine the validity of an election, appointment, removal or resignation and the right of any person to hold or continue to hold the office; to determine the person entitled to an office claimed by more than 1 person; to make such order or decree as may be just and proper, with power to enforce the production of books, papers and records of the corporation relating to the issue; to order an election to be held in accordance with section 211 or section 215; to make such order respecting further or other notice of the application as it deems proper
      `an application under subsection (a) is before the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an application under section 225(a) before the Court?
      `the Court determines that no valid election has been held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court determined that no valid election has been held?
      `the office is claimed by more than 1 person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the office claimed by more than one person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `What can the Court of Chancery do on an application about an election (s 225(a))` IF
    `s 225(a) the Court of Chancery may exercise the power on the application` `the power` `an application under subsection (a) is before the Court` `the Court determines that no valid election has been held` `the office is claimed by more than 1 person`

@export Can the Court of Chancery remove me from office as a director (s 225(c))?
GIVEN `I have been convicted of a felony in connection with my duties to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of a felony in connection with your duties as a director to the corporation?
      `a court has found on the merits that I breached the duty of loyalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court of competent jurisdiction given a prior judgment on the merits that you breached the duty of loyalty in connection with your duties to the corporation?
      `the application is by the corporation or derivatively by a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made by the corporation, or derivatively in the right of the corporation by a stockholder?
      `the application is in a subsequent action brought for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made in a subsequent action brought for the purpose of your removal?
      `the Court determines that I did not act in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court determined that you did not act in good faith in performing the acts that resulted in the conviction or judgment?
      `the Court determines that removal is necessary to avoid irreparable harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court determined that judicial removal is necessary to avoid irreparable harm to the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Court of Chancery remove me from office as a director (s 225(c))` IF
    `s 225(c) the Court of Chancery may remove the director from office` `the application`
    WHERE
        `the application` MEANS `dg5 s 225(c) Application to remove a director` WITH
              `the director has been convicted of a felony in connection with the duties of the director to the corporation` IS `I have been convicted of a felony in connection with my duties to the corporation`
            , `there has been a prior judgment on the merits by a court of competent jurisdiction that the director has committed a breach of the duty of loyalty in connection with the duties of the director to the corporation` IS `a court has found on the merits that I breached the duty of loyalty`
            , `the application is made by the corporation, or derivatively in the right of the corporation by a stockholder` IS `the application is by the corporation or derivatively by a stockholder`
            , `the application is made in a subsequent action brought for such purpose` IS `the application is in a subsequent action brought for that purpose`
            , `the Court determines that the director did not act in good faith in performing the acts resulting in the prior conviction or judgment` IS `the Court determines that I did not act in good faith`
            , `the Court determines that judicial removal is necessary to avoid irreparable harm to the corporation` IS `the Court determines that removal is necessary to avoid irreparable harm`

§ `Section 226 -- a custodian or receiver for a deadlocked or abandoned corporation`

GIVEN s IS A BOOLEAN
      g1 IS A BOOLEAN
      g2 IS A BOOLEAN
      g2b IS A BOOLEAN
      g3 IS A BOOLEAN
      g3b IS A BOOLEAN
      i IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `dg5 s 226(a) Application for a custodian`
`dg5 seat custodian application` s g1 g2 g2b g3 g3b i MEANS
    `dg5 s 226(a) Application for a custodian` WITH
          `the applicant is a stockholder` IS s
        , `at a meeting held for the election of directors the stockholders are so divided that they have failed to elect successors to directors whose terms have expired or would have expired upon qualification of their successors` IS g1
        , `the business of the corporation is suffering or is threatened with irreparable injury because the directors are so divided that the required vote for action by the board cannot be obtained` IS g2
        , `the stockholders are unable to terminate that division` IS g2b
        , `the corporation has abandoned its business` IS g3
        , `the corporation has failed within a reasonable time to take steps to dissolve, liquidate or distribute its assets` IS g3b
        , `the corporation is insolvent` IS i

@export May I, as a stockholder, ask the Court of Chancery to appoint a custodian for the corporation (s 226(a))?
GIVEN `the stockholders failed to elect directors at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At a meeting held for the election of directors, are the stockholders so divided that they have failed to elect successors to directors whose terms have expired?
      `the business is suffering because the directors are deadlocked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation's business suffering, or threatened with irreparable injury, because the directors are so divided that the required vote for board action cannot be obtained?
      `the stockholders cannot end the directors' division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the stockholders unable to terminate that division?
      `the corporation has abandoned its business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation abandoned its business?
      `the corporation has not taken steps to dissolve in a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it failed, within a reasonable time, to take steps to dissolve, liquidate or distribute its assets?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as a stockholder, ask the Court of Chancery to appoint a custodian for the corporation (s 226(a))` IF
    `s 226(a) a ground exists on which the Court of Chancery may appoint a custodian`
        (`dg5 seat custodian application` TRUE `the stockholders failed to elect directors at a meeting` `the business is suffering because the directors are deadlocked` `the stockholders cannot end the directors' division` `the corporation has abandoned its business` `the corporation has not taken steps to dissolve in a reasonable time`
            -- Placeholder: the ground rule does not read insolvency.
            FALSE)

@export May the Court of Chancery appoint a receiver for the corporation as well (s 226(a))?
GIVEN `the stockholders failed to elect directors at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At a meeting held for the election of directors, are the stockholders so divided that they have failed to elect successors to directors whose terms have expired?
      `the business is suffering because the directors are deadlocked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation's business suffering, or threatened with irreparable injury, because the directors are so divided that the required vote for board action cannot be obtained?
      `the stockholders cannot end the directors' division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the stockholders unable to terminate that division?
      `the corporation has abandoned its business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation abandoned its business?
      `the corporation has not taken steps to dissolve in a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it failed, within a reasonable time, to take steps to dissolve, liquidate or distribute its assets?
      `the corporation is insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation insolvent?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court of Chancery appoint a receiver for the corporation as well (s 226(a))` IF
    `s 226(a) the Court of Chancery may appoint a receiver as well`
        (`dg5 seat custodian application` TRUE `the stockholders failed to elect directors at a meeting` `the business is suffering because the directors are deadlocked` `the stockholders cannot end the directors' division` `the corporation has abandoned its business` `the corporation has not taken steps to dissolve in a reasonable time` `the corporation is insolvent`)

@export Is a custodian's authority limited to continuing the business (s 226(b))?
GIVEN `the Court has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court of Chancery ordered otherwise?
      `the appointment is for abandonment under s 226(a)(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appointment for a corporation that has abandoned its business and failed to take steps to dissolve (section 226(a)(3))?
      `the appointment arises under s 352(a)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the appointment arise under section 352(a)(2) (a close corporation)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a custodian's authority limited to continuing the business (s 226(b))` IF
    `s 226(b) the custodian's authority is to continue the business and not to liquidate its affairs` `the Court has ordered otherwise` `the appointment is for abandonment under s 226(a)(3)` `the appointment arises under s 352(a)(2)`

@export By when must I give the Attorney General a copy of my application for a custodian (s 226(c))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a stock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a stock corporation (one authorized to issue capital stock)?
      `the corporation is a charitable nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a nonstock corporation, is it a charitable nonstock corporation (a nonprofit nonstock corporation exempt under section 501(c)(3) of the Internal Revenue Code)?
      `the date I filed the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the application with the Court of Chancery? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By when must I give the Attorney General a copy of my application for a custodian (s 226(c))` IS
    `s 226(c) the last day for the applicant to provide a copy to the Attorney General` (`dg5 seat the kind of corporation` `the corporation is a stock corporation` `the corporation is a charitable nonstock corporation`) `the date I filed the application`

@export Did I give the Attorney General the copy in time (s 226(c))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a stock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a stock corporation (one authorized to issue capital stock)?
      `the corporation is a charitable nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a nonstock corporation, is it a charitable nonstock corporation (a nonprofit nonstock corporation exempt under section 501(c)(3) of the Internal Revenue Code)?
      `the date I filed the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the application with the Court of Chancery? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
      `I have given the Attorney General a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the Attorney General a copy of the application?
      `the date I gave the Attorney General the copy` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (ISO 8601; any date if you have not)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I give the Attorney General the copy in time (s 226(c))` IS
    `s 226(c) the applicant provided the copy to the Attorney General in time` (`dg5 seat the kind of corporation` `the corporation is a stock corporation` `the corporation is a charitable nonstock corporation`) `the date I filed the application`
        (IF `I have given the Attorney General a copy` THEN JUST `the date I gave the Attorney General the copy` ELSE NOTHING)

§ `Section 227 -- the Court's powers in elections of directors`

GIVEN s211 IS A BOOLEAN
      s215 IS A BOOLEAN
      s225 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `dg5 s 227 Proceeding in the Court of Chancery`
`dg5 seat proceeding` s211 s215 s225 MEANS
    IF s211
    THEN `a proceeding instituted under section 211`
    ELSE IF s215
         THEN `a proceeding instituted under section 215`
         ELSE IF s225
              THEN `a proceeding instituted under section 225`
              ELSE `a proceeding not instituted under section 211, 215 or 225`

@export Can the Court of Chancery decide whether I have the right to vote my stock in an election proceeding (s 227(a))?
GIVEN `the proceeding is under section 211` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding one under section 211 (meetings of stockholders)?
      `the proceeding is under section 215` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding one under section 215 (nonstock corporations)?
      `the proceeding is under section 225` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding one under section 225 (contested elections)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Court of Chancery decide whether I have the right to vote my stock in an election proceeding (s 227(a))` IF
    `s 227(a) the Court of Chancery may determine the right and power of a person claiming to own stock to vote` (`dg5 seat proceeding` `the proceeding is under section 211` `the proceeding is under section 215` `the proceeding is under section 225`)

@export Can the Court of Chancery appoint a magistrate to hold the election (s 227(b))?
GIVEN `the proceeding is under section 211` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding one under section 211 (meetings of stockholders)?
      `the proceeding is under section 215` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding one under section 215 (nonstock corporations)?
      `the proceeding is under section 225` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding one under section 225 (contested elections)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Court of Chancery appoint a magistrate to hold the election (s 227(b))` IF
    `s 227(b) the Court of Chancery may appoint a Magistrate in Chancery to hold the election` (`dg5 seat proceeding` `the proceeding is under section 211` `the proceeding is under section 215` `the proceeding is under section 225`)

@export Can the Court of Chancery punish me for contempt if I disobey its order as an officer or director (s 227(b))?
GIVEN `I disobeyed an order made by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, as an officer or director, disobey an order made by the Court of Chancery?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Court of Chancery punish me for contempt if I disobey its order as an officer or director (s 227(b))` IF
    `s 227(b) the Court of Chancery may punish the officer or director for contempt` `I disobeyed an order made by the Court`

@export What is the most the Court of Chancery may fine the corporation for disobeying its order, in dollars (s 227(b))?
GIVEN `the corporation disobeyed an order made by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation disobey an order made by the Court of Chancery?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the Court of Chancery may fine the corporation for disobeying its order, in dollars (s 227(b))` IS
    `s 227(b) the most the Court of Chancery may enter against the corporation as a penalty, in dollars` `the corporation disobeyed an order made by the Court`

§ `Section 228 -- action by written consent in place of a meeting`

-- Helper: the consent as the layer-1 module expects it, from the person's answers.
GIVEN fm IS A BOOLEAN
      wy IS A `dg5 s 228(d)(1) Way a consent is delivered`
      hm IS A BOOLEAN
      pp IS A BOOLEAN
      ds IS A BOOLEAN
      inf IS A BOOLEAN
      px IS A BOOLEAN
      pxo IS A BOOLEAN
      dd IS A DATE
      fu IS A BOOLEAN
      di IS A DATE
      df IS A DATE
      ev IS A BOOLEAN
      h1 IS A BOOLEAN
      h2 IS A BOOLEAN
      rv IS A BOOLEAN
      ir IS A BOOLEAN
      vt IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `dg5 s 228 Consent delivered to the corporation`
`dg5 seat consent` fm wy hm pp ds inf px pxo dd fu di df ev h1 h2 rv ir vt MEANS
    `dg5 s 228 Consent delivered to the corporation` WITH
          `the consent is set forth in writing or in an electronic transmission` IS fm
        , `the way the consent was delivered` IS wy
        , `the consent was delivered by hand or by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested` IS hm
        , `the consent was reproduced and delivered in paper form` IS pp
        , `the corporation has designated the information processing system` IS ds
        , `the consent sets forth or is delivered with information that enables the corporation to determine the date of delivery and the identity of the person giving it` IS inf
        , `the consent is given by a person authorized to act for a stockholder or member as proxy` IS px
        , `that proxy's consent complies with s 212(c)(2) and (3)` IS pxo
        , `the date on which the consent was delivered to the corporation` IS dd
        , `the consent is to be effective at a future time` IS fu
        , `the date on which the instruction or provision for the future time was given` IS di
        , `the date of the future time at which the consent is to be effective` IS df
        , `evidence of the instruction or provision for the future time was provided to the corporation` IS ev
        , `the signer was a stockholder or member of record when the consent was executed` IS h1
        , `the signer was a stockholder or member of record on the record date for determining those entitled to consent to the action` IS h2
        , `the consent was revoked before it became effective` IS rv
        , `the consent is made irrevocable by a provision otherwise providing` IS ir
        , `the number of votes the consent carries` IS vt

-- s 228(a), (b). Stockholders of a stock corporation, or members of a nonstock corporation, may act without a meeting, notice or vote if consents carry at least
-- the votes the action would need at a meeting at which everyone entitled to vote was present and voted. The vote the action needs is asked as a fraction in whole numbers.
@export Can the stockholders or members take this action by written consent, without a meeting (s 228(a), (b))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a stock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a stock corporation (one authorized to issue capital stock)? Answer no for a nonstock corporation.
      `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation provide that action may not be taken by consent?
      `the action needs this many parts` IS A NUMBER @desc At a meeting at which everyone entitled to vote was present and voted, the action would need a fraction of the votes: what is the top of that fraction? (for a majority: 1)
      `out of this many parts` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the bottom of that fraction? (for a majority: 2; for two-thirds: 3)
      `the votes must exceed that fraction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must the votes exceed that fraction (as for "a majority"), rather than only reach it (as for "at least two-thirds")?
      `the votes carried by the consents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes do the consents carry (of the stockholders or members who signed and delivered them in the way the section requires)?
      `the votes entitled to be cast on the action` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are entitled to be cast on the action in all?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the stockholders or members take this action by written consent, without a meeting (s 228(a), (b))` IS
    IF `out of this many parts` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN IF `the corporation is a stock corporation`
         THEN `s 228(a) the stockholders may take the action without a meeting, without prior notice and without a vote` `dg5 seat the stock kind` `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` `the vote the action needs` `the votes carried by the consents` `the votes entitled to be cast on the action`
         ELSE `s 228(b) the members may take the action without a meeting, without prior notice and without a vote` `dg5 seat the nonstock kind` `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` `the vote the action needs` `the votes carried by the consents` `the votes entitled to be cast on the action`
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `dg5 seat the stock kind` MEANS `a stock corporation`
        `dg5 seat the nonstock kind` MEANS `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`
        `the vote the action needs` MEANS
            `Vote requirement` WITH `counted against` IS `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`
                                  , proportion IS `the action needs this many parts` DIVIDED BY `out of this many parts`
                                  , `must be exceeded` IS `the votes must exceed that fraction`

@export Is my written consent a consent that section 228 permits (s 228(c), (d))?
GIVEN `my consent is set forth in writing or in an electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your consent set forth in writing or in an electronic transmission?
      `I delivered it` IS A `dg5 s 228(d)(1) Way a consent is delivered` @desc How did you deliver it? One of: to the principal place of business of the corporation; to an officer or agent of the corporation having custody of the book in which proceedings of meetings of stockholders or members are recorded; to the registered office of the corporation in this State; to an information processing system designated by the corporation for receiving consents, in accordance with section 116
      `I delivered it by hand or by certified or registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you delivered it to the registered office, was it by hand or by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested?
      `it was reproduced and delivered in paper form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it reproduced and delivered in paper form?
      `the corporation designated that system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you delivered it to an information processing system, had the corporation designated that system for receiving consents?
      `it enables the corporation to tell the date and who gave it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the consent set forth, or come with, information that enables the corporation to determine the date of delivery and who gave it?
      `I gave it as a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give it as a person authorized to act for a stockholder or member as proxy?
      `my proxy consent complies with s 212(c)(2) and (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you gave it as a proxy, does it comply with section 212(c)(2) and (3)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my written consent a consent that section 228 permits (s 228(c), (d))` IF
    `s 228(c) the consent is a consent permitted by this section`
        (`dg5 seat consent` `my consent is set forth in writing or in an electronic transmission` `I delivered it` `I delivered it by hand or by certified or registered mail` `it was reproduced and delivered in paper form` `the corporation designated that system` `it enables the corporation to tell the date and who gave it` `I gave it as a proxy` `my proxy consent complies with s 212(c)(2) and (3)`
            -- Placeholders: the permission rule reads none of the remaining ten fields.
            (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0)

@export Does my written consent count toward the action (s 228(c))?
GIVEN `my consent is set forth in writing or in an electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your consent set forth in writing or in an electronic transmission?
      `I delivered it` IS A `dg5 s 228(d)(1) Way a consent is delivered` @desc How did you deliver it? One of: to the principal place of business of the corporation; to an officer or agent of the corporation having custody of the book in which proceedings of meetings of stockholders or members are recorded; to the registered office of the corporation in this State; to an information processing system designated by the corporation for receiving consents, in accordance with section 116
      `I delivered it by hand or by certified or registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you delivered it to the registered office, was it by hand or by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested?
      `it was reproduced and delivered in paper form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it reproduced and delivered in paper form?
      `the corporation designated that system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you delivered it to an information processing system, had the corporation designated that system for receiving consents?
      `it enables the corporation to tell the date and who gave it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the consent set forth, or come with, information that enables the corporation to determine the date of delivery and who gave it?
      `I gave it as a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give it as a person authorized to act for a stockholder or member as proxy?
      `my proxy consent complies with s 212(c)(2) and (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you gave it as a proxy, does it comply with section 212(c)(2) and (3)?
      `the date I delivered it` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your consent delivered to the corporation? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-10)
      `the first date any consent was delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the first consent delivered to the corporation for this action? (ISO 8601)
      `my consent is to take effect at a future time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide that your consent will be effective at a future time (including on the happening of an event)?
      `the date I gave that instruction` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did you give the instruction or make the provision? (ISO 8601; any date if not)
      `the date of that future time` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date is the future time (or the event expected to occur)? (ISO 8601; any date if not)
      `I gave the corporation evidence of that instruction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the corporation evidence of that instruction or provision?
      `I was a holder of record when I signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a stockholder or member of record when you executed the consent?
      `I was a holder of record on the record date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a stockholder or member of record on the record date for determining those entitled to consent to the action?
      `I revoked my consent before it took effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you revoke your consent before it became effective?
      `my consent was made irrevocable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your consent made irrevocable by a provision that says otherwise than the Law's default (that a consent is revocable before it becomes effective)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my written consent count toward the action (s 228(c))` IF
    `s 228(c) the consent counts toward the action` `my consent` `the first date any consent was delivered`
    WHERE
        `my consent` MEANS
            (`dg5 seat consent` `my consent is set forth in writing or in an electronic transmission` `I delivered it` `I delivered it by hand or by certified or registered mail` `it was reproduced and delivered in paper form` `the corporation designated that system` `it enables the corporation to tell the date and who gave it` `I gave it as a proxy` `my proxy consent complies with s 212(c)(2) and (3)` `the date I delivered it` `my consent is to take effect at a future time` `the date I gave that instruction` `the date of that future time` `I gave the corporation evidence of that instruction` `I was a holder of record when I signed` `I was a holder of record on the record date` `I revoked my consent before it took effect` `my consent was made irrevocable`
                -- Placeholder: the number of votes the consent carries is not read by this rule.
                0)

@export By when must consents carrying enough votes be delivered (s 228(c))?
GIVEN `the first date any consent was delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the first consent delivered to the corporation for this action? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must consents carrying enough votes be delivered (s 228(c))` IS
    `s 228(c) the last day for sufficient consents to be delivered` `the first date any consent was delivered`

@export Is my revocation of my consent effective (s 228(c))?
GIVEN `I revoked my consent before it took effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you revoke your consent before it became effective?
      `my consent was made irrevocable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your consent made irrevocable by a provision that says otherwise than the Law's default (that a consent is revocable before it becomes effective)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my revocation of my consent effective (s 228(c))` IF
    `s 228(c) the consent was effectively revoked`
        (`dg5 seat consent`
